## Context

PR #1209 merged on 2026-10-06 as `e02cd208b5f9cbe9b60fe556d7dff835702fc1a4`.
Its validator now stops at the first broken projection and prints a general
refusal directing the operator to `idh install`. Three existing tests still
require the refusal to include `double-fire` or `claude-code` for their
specific broken fixtures. On `origin/main` at `bd2efaad7cbf0a44d57545a68ebf9394aaef8157`,
the documentation-only PR #1216 ran `make check`: 3 failed, 1491 passed,
2 skipped. A targeted rerun reproduced the same three failures, with 75
other validator tests deselected. `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- scripts tests
adapters` is empty on PR #1216; this is an integrated-main failure, not a
change introduced by that wrap-up.

The failed tests are
`test_stale_harness_hooks_in_live_settings_block_the_launch`,
`test_a_missing_plugin_link_blocks_the_launch`, and
`test_a_hand_copied_plugin_block_also_blocks_the_launch` in
`tests/test_projection_validator.py`. Each still sees exit 1, but the stderr
is the generic `idh: refusing to launch claude: harness projections are
incomplete; run idh install ...` line instead of the asserted defect name.
The intended detail contract after PR #1209 needs reconciliation; no change
to the launch refusal's fail-closed behavior is requested here.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Decide whether the post-1209 launch refusal should name the specific
      broken projection or whether the tests should assert the intended
      generic install direction; document the intended operator-visible
      message in the relevant code or test.
- [x] All three named tests pass, with a positive control that a broken
      projection still refuses launch and a healthy projection still launches.
- [x] `make check` passes on the resolved integration branch.

## Resolution

Ticket 1040 in merged PR #1215 chose the generic installer direction and
updated the three existing assertions only. It preserved refusal for invalid
hook/plugin configurations and retained the clean-settings and operator-hook
positive controls. Its focused validator suite passed 78 tests; full `make
check` passed 1494 tests with 2 skipped, and all ten PR CI jobs succeeded.
This ticket had not commissioned a separate implementation before that merge.
